      <description align="center" color="red" colored="true" height="572" resized="true" width="360" x="21" y="16">Prepare Optimizer Objectives&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Author:&lt;br&gt;Akshay Hasabe&lt;br&gt;Naveen Kumar&lt;br&gt;Karthik Sanagapalli&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Overview:&lt;br&gt;This block reads the objective table and joins it with model_tag and tag_details to fetch the name and formula_expression for each objective tag. This information is used to define the logic and intent of each objective. The prepared objectives are then passed to the Gekko optimizer to guide the optimization process toward targets like cost minimization or efficiency maximization.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Inputs:&lt;br&gt;I/P 1: objective&lt;br&gt;I/P 2: model_tag&lt;br&gt;I/P 3: tag_details&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Output:&lt;br&gt;O/P1: objective&lt;br&gt;O/P 2: objective&lt;br&gt;tag name&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;</description>
